THE FLESH AND BONE LICENSE
Version 1.0 - November 2026

Copyright (c) 2026 megalith (Rick Collette, megalith@root.sh)

This tool is here so people can learn from it. Read it. Tear it apart. Change
it. Make something weird. Give it away. Sell it. I don't care.

There is one hard rule: use AI to write programs in exBASIC if you want. Do
not use it to write exBASIC itself.

1. DEFINITIONS

"Software" means exBASIC Studio and the original source code, documentation,
art, music, level data and other material distributed under this license. It
does not include separately licensed third-party material.

"User Program" means a program, game, application, source file, asset or other
work created to be compiled, assembled, packaged, run or otherwise processed
with the Software. A User Program is not part of the Software merely because
the Software was used to create or process it.

"Generative AI" means a machine-learning system that generates or materially
rewrites code, text, images, audio or other expressive material in response to
prompts, examples, training data or supplied context. Compilers, assemblers,
linkers, debuggers, formatters, converters, compression tools, build systems
and deterministic generators are not Generative AI merely because they are
software.

2. WHAT YOU CAN DO

Permission is granted, free of charge, to use, run, study, copy, modify,
publish, distribute, sublicense and sell the Software and its source, art,
music, level data and other included material, subject to the rule below.

3. AI IS FINE FOR YOUR PROGRAMS

Use Generative AI to write, change, debug or explain your User Program if you
want. Generate a whole game, ask it to fix a compiler error or have it make
data tables. That code is yours to publish, give away or sell.

This is still true when the User Program is written in exBASIC, built by
exBASIC Studio or informed by the exBASIC language manual.

This exception does not permit Generative AI to generate or materially rewrite
the Software itself or a derivative work based on the Software.

4. THE NO-AI RULE FOR THE SOFTWARE

You may not publish, distribute, sublicense, sell or otherwise release a copy,
modification or derivative work of the Software containing code,
documentation, art, music, writing, level data or other material generated or
materially rewritten by Generative AI.

You may not use the Software or a protected part of it as training data,
prompt context, an example to imitate or other input to Generative AI for the
purpose of creating, modifying or materially rewriting the Software or a
derivative work of it.

Private experiments are your business. Releasing the result is not allowed.

5. HUMAN WORK IS FINE

Human-written changes and human-made derivative works are allowed. That is the
point. You may learn from the Software and use what you learned in your own
work. You may also use general ideas, facts, methods, interfaces and game
mechanics that copyright law does not protect.

This license does not claim ownership of abstract ideas or concepts. It covers
the actual code, text, art, music, characters, levels and specific creative
expression found in the Software.

6. KEEP THIS LICENSE

Any copy or substantial portion of the Software that you release must include
this license and the copyright notice above. You may add your own copyright
notice for your own human-made work, but you may not remove or weaken the
No-AI Rule for material covered by this license.

7. IF YOU BREAK THE RULE

Your permission under this license ends automatically if you break the No-AI
Rule. It is restored only after every violating release is removed and every
copy you control is destroyed.

8. NO WARRANTY

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGE OR OTHER
LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,
OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE
SOFTWARE.

9. IF ONE PART FAILS

If a court decides that one part of this license cannot be enforced, the rest
still applies as far as the law allows.

This license applies only to original exBASIC Studio material that is not
separately licensed. It does not relicense the third-party exBASIC handbook
copied into internal/manual/chapters/.

The separately built `mkatr-go` executable and its implementation under
